@swyc520/dsh-plugin-model-whitelist README · 桌面端 / DSHEAC AIO：桌面端的 profile 由 Electron 应用独占，命令行 `dsh plugin add` 无法写入。请在应用内的
插件管理器里安装；若手工安装，注意桌面端的 profile 闸门**不允许 `link:` 依赖或目录 junction**，
必须是真实目录。

@swyc520/dsh-plugin-model-whitelist README · Collapsing a group：> If the panel says no catalog has been read yet, open the model selector once. The
> catalog is loaded on demand by the official model-selection plugin, and this plugin
> reads that same catalog.

@swyc520/dsh-plugin-model-whitelist README · The whitelist lives in browser local storage：It persists the *hidden* set rather than the *shown* set, so a model the user has
never seen — a new release, a newly connected provider — is visible by default.
Persisting the shown set would silently hide every new model, which reads as a bug.

@swyc520/dsh-plugin-model-whitelist README · The filter is a projection, not a shadow：- the official component renders its **own** UI as before, over a list that no longer
  contains the hidden models;
- the real store is never written to, and `subscribe` still reports the real changes,
  so both catalog updates and whitelist edits trigger a re-render;
- the projection is idempotent and total: it copies only the `groups` array, and only
  when something is actually hidden.

The original method is restored when the plugin is disposed.

@swyc520/dsh-plugin-model-whitelist README · Compatibility：Verified on **dsh `0.2.0-rc.2`** (desktop @deepseek-ai/dsh-desktop 0.2.0-rc.2,
Electron 44, Node 24.18.1): the panel appears, unticking a model removes it from the
selector menu immediately, and ticking it back restores it.
